        <div class="section recommendations" id="recommendations">
            <h2>Strategic Recommendations</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <h4>1. Re-evaluate Deep Discount Strategies</h4>
                    <p>Since data shows almost zero correlation between discount depth and customer rating ({discount_rating_corr:.3f}), management should test reducing discount depths on high-performing categories to preserve margin without sacrificing customer satisfaction.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <h4>2. Prune Underperforming Categories</h4>
                    <p>Categories consistently scoring lower average ratings despite high promotional intensity should undergo aggressive assortment review. Remove consistently defective products driving the "waste" and "poor" sentiment keywords.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <h4>3. Leverage Highly-Engaged Products for Cross-Selling</h4>
                    <p>With a median rating count of {med_rating_count:,.0f} and several products significantly exceeding this, capitalize on high-traffic, highly-rated items by grouping them with related higher-margin accessories.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <h4>4. Quality Control on "Defective" Flags</h4>
                    <p>Address the specific products driving the "defective" and "broken" keywords. Establishing a threshold (e.g., dropping products that fall below a 3.5 rating) will maintain the current {high_rating_share:.1f}% high-rating share and protect brand trust.</p>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

    </div>
</body>
